%N A259707 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of permutations of {1,...,n} starting with 1 and having exactly k overlaps, for n >= 1 and 0 <= k <= floor((n-2)^2/4).
%C A259707 Following Sade (Section 2), we count only permutations starting with 1. - _Seiichi Manyama_, Nov 04 2026
%D A259707 A. Sade, Sur les Chevauchements des Permutations, published by the author, Marseille, 1949.
